---
Rebuilds the existing typecheck's input from the new discovery stage's tables.
This is the only module that knows both shapes: it reads the stage's frozen
tables and builds the parsed AST, module identities, surfaces and graph the
existing front end's typecheck consumes. It is a transformation only: it lexes,
parses, resolves and checks nothing, and a fact the tables lack is a gap to fix
in the stage, not here.

It shrinks as typecheck is rewritten to read the tables, and it is deleted
when typecheck takes `FrontendTables` directly.

Declarations only so far: signatures, types, imports, foreign blocks and
docstrings are rebuilt, and every function or method body and every global's
value is the placeholder `DECLARATION_ONLY_BODY` until the body half lands
(`docs/DISCOVERY_ACCEPTANCE_ROADMAP.md`, item 4).

A row the tables should hold and do not is a `LegacyAdapterError`, never a
default: no placeholder value flows into the rebuilt AST. The freeze
invariants make such a row unreachable for tables a stage run froze, so an
error means the stage or the adapter is wrong, and the differential fails on it.
Reads of text by an id the invariants checked (a name, a literal, a path) use
the stage's total accessors, whose fallbacks are unreachable for the same
reason.
---
import:
	../compiler_new/stage_01_discovery/sources/embedded_standard_library:
		EmbeddedStandardLibraryTexts,
		embedded_module_name,
	../compiler_new/stage_01_discovery/sources/source_provider: SOURCE_FILE_EXTENSION
